  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Saturday)\nIssued at 1237 PM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nMain forecast concern through the extended period will be the\nridge of high pressure holding across the Plains through the first\nhalf of next week. At the same time, the low level thermal ridge\nis progged to expand eastward as well which will continue a slow\nwarming trend through Tuesday over the CWA. Forecast high\ntemperatures in the upper 90s to around 104 degrees are\nanticipated each afternoon into Tuesday. Surface low pressure\nbuilds lee of the Rocky Mountains Monday allowing for an increase\nin south/southwesterly winds. This should help to mix dewpoints\nout a little more compared to today/Sunday. In response, heat \nindex values each afternoon look to reach advisory levels through \nremaining mostly below warning criteria. \n\nLatest model solutions continue to highlight the ridge retreating\nwestward for the second half of next week. This puts the CWA back\non the eastern periphery of the ridge with the potential for a\ncouple shortwaves to slide southeast through the Plains. A weak\nfrontal boundary could sag into the region Wednesday and remain in\nthe area ahead of a more defined shortwave currently progged to\nmove into the region next weekend. Uncertainties remain with where\nthis boundary sets up and the overall timing of these waves. For\nnow will continue with slight chances for convection each\nafternoon/evening Wednesday to Saturday.",
